<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>9.2. Classes on iOS UIKit Course</title><link>/docs/9.-creating-your-own-data-types/9.2.-classes/</link><description>Recent content in 9.2. Classes on iOS UIKit Course</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="/docs/9.-creating-your-own-data-types/9.2.-classes/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>9.2.1. Inheritance</title><link>/docs/9.-creating-your-own-data-types/9.2.-classes/9.2.1.-inheritance/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/9.-creating-your-own-data-types/9.2.-classes/9.2.1.-inheritance/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="921-inheritance"&gt;9.2.1. Inheritance&lt;a class="anchor" href="#921-inheritance"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One of the most critical capabilities that a class has but a struct doesn&amp;rsquo;t have is inheritance.&lt;/strong&gt; Inheritance is the ability of a class to inherit the properties of another existing class and add more functionalities along with it. In other words, we can build a new class based on another existing class. For example, we can build a new class &lt;code&gt;Car&lt;/code&gt; based on the &lt;code&gt;Vehicle&lt;/code&gt; class we have:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>9.2.2. Value vs. Reference</title><link>/docs/9.-creating-your-own-data-types/9.2.-classes/9.2.2.-value-vs.-reference/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/9.-creating-your-own-data-types/9.2.-classes/9.2.2.-value-vs.-reference/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="922-value-vs-reference"&gt;9.2.2. Value vs. Reference&lt;a class="anchor" href="#922-value-vs-reference"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another major difference between a struct and a class is how they behave when copied. Structs are &amp;lsquo;value types,&amp;rsquo; and classes are &amp;lsquo;reference types.&amp;rsquo;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;mark style="color:purple;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(Structs)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/mark&gt; When you copy an instance of a struct from an existing instance, both instances work independently. For example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;{
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; name:String
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//creating an instance of User...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; user1 = User(name: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;John Smith&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//copying the instance to a new instance...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; user2 = user1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//changing the name in the copied instance...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;user2.name = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Bob Smith&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; User name of user1 = &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;user1.name&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; User name of user2 = &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;user2.name&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; &amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>